{"title":"Writing plural forms of nouns","key_idea":"Most nouns add -es or -s to show more than one, but some nouns have special plural forms you must learn by heart.","method":["Look at how the noun ends","If it ends in x, z, s, sh, or ch, add -es","If it ends in a consonant and y, change y to i and add -es","Some nouns like child and leaf have special plural forms that do not follow the rule"],"worked_example":{"problem":"Write the plural of box, child, leaf","steps":["box ends in x, so add -es: boxes","child is special, the plural is children","leaf is special, the plural is leaves"],"answer":"boxes, children, leaves"},"key_terms":[{"term":"plural","meaning":"more than one of something"},{"term":"singular","meaning":"one of something"}],"common_mistakes":["Writing childs or leafs instead of the correct special forms children and leaves","Forgetting to add -es to words ending in x, z, s, sh, or ch"],"remember":"Most nouns add -s or -es, but always check special nouns like child, leaf, person, tooth.","quick_check":[{"q":"What is the plural of box?","a":"boxes"},{"q":"What is the plural of child?","a":"children"}],"tell_your_child":"When you write plural, think about how the word ends. If it ends in x like box, add -es to make boxes. Some words like child and leaf are tricky and have their own special plural forms that you need to remember."}
